# /etc/default/earlyoom — userspace OOM killer config (#175)
#
# Why this is needed at all: exe.dev session processes inherit oom_score_adj
# -1000 from exe-init/sshd, so the kernel OOM killer can NEVER pick the agent
# session or anything it launches. Under real exhaustion it takes the host's
# production service instead. earlyoom acts *before* the kernel does and can
# be told what to prefer, which the kernel killer cannot.
#
# -r 3600     report memory state hourly (journal), not every 60s
# -m 6,3      warn at 6% free RAM, kill at 3%. No -s: this host has no swap.
# --avoid     never pick the web app, sshd, or PID-1-ish supervisors.
# --prefer    pick the transient npm/node installs first — the measured peak
#             on this class of host was a cold `npx socraticode@latest`
#             install (1.2 G at the cgroup), not the indexing that follows.
#
# NB earlyoom 1.7 floors a --prefer match's effective score at 300, so this
# only works while wslcb-web.service sits BELOW 300; its OOMScoreAdjust=-700
# puts it at ~208. Changing one without the other silently re-arms the bug.
#
# NB2 these match /proc/<pid>/comm, which the kernel TRUNCATES to 15 chars —
# the npm launch shows up as 'npm exec socrat', not 'npm'. Do not anchor these
# with a trailing '$': it makes --prefer match nothing at all, and lets
# sshd-session and systemd-journal slip past --avoid. Verified against
# `ps -eo comm=` on this host.
# VALIDATED against earlyoom v1.7 on this host, 2026-09-19: the daemon echoed
# back both regexes and the 6%/3% thresholds. Re-check after any edit — a
# malformed EARLYOOM_ARGS fails at start, during an incident, on the one
# mechanism meant to handle it.
#
# `apt install earlyoom` starts the daemon BEFORE this file is in place, and
# `systemctl enable --now` will not restart an already-active unit — so the
# stock `-r 3600` (no regexes, 10%/5%) stays loaded while the unit reports
# active and enabled. Always restart, then read the journal, never infer from
# unit state:
#   sudo systemctl restart earlyoom
#   journalctl -u earlyoom -n 12 --no-pager   # must print BOTH regex lines
#                                             # and 6.00% / 3.00%
EARLYOOM_ARGS="-r 3600 -m 6,3 --avoid '^(uvicorn|sshd|systemd|exe-init)' --prefer '^(node|npm|npx)'"
